d 'SEGMCOINT': module to provide tests for segmented cointegration (cointegration holding only over part of the sample)
d
d	  segmcoint implements three complementary residual-based
d procedures that test the null of    no cointegration over the
d whole sample against the alternative that a stable   
d cointegrating relationship prevails over one or more subperiods,
d while breaking down	 (nonstationary error) over others.  This
d situation - segmented cointegration - was    introduced by Kim
d (2003) and explains why standard full-sample Engle-Granger /	 
d Phillips-Ouliaris tests often fail to confirm a well understood
d long-run relationship: a    relatively short interval of
d nonstationary deviation can dominate the full-sample	  statistic
d and mask the relationship. 
d
d KW: cointegration
d KW: tests
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260727
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
f segmcoint.ado
f segmcoint.sthlp
f segmcoint_dm.sthlp
f segmcoint_example.do
f segmcoint_kim.sthlp
f segmcoint_methods.sthlp
f segmcoint_mr.sthlp
